      "category": "C3",
      "title": "Class runs without sharing",
      "severity": "Medium",
      "file": "CaseHistoryController.cls",
      "lines": "1",
      "explanation": "The class is declared 'without sharing', which means it ignores record-level sharing settings. This can allow users to access Case records they shouldn't be able to see based on their sharing rules or roles.",
      "remediation": "Change the class declaration from 'without sharing' to 'with sharing' or 'inherited sharing' to enforce record-level sharing."
    },
    {
      "category": "C2",
      "title": "FLS not enforced in query results",
      "severity": "Medium",
      "file": "CaseHistoryController.cls",
      "lines": "10",
      "explanation": "While Security.stripInaccessible is used, it's applied after the query. The query itself does not enforce FLS, which means fields that the user shouldn't have access to might be included in the initial query results before stripping.",
      "remediation": "Use WITH SECURITY_ENFORCED or WITH USER_MODE in the SOQL query to enforce FLS at query time, rather than relying solely on Security.stripInaccessible."
    }
  ]
}

